From: Adarsh Jagadish Kamini <adarsh.jagadish.kamini@est.tech>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: use DW_CFLAGS to look for elfutils/version.h

The check for elfutils/version.h adds -I$EU_INCLUDEDIR to CPPFLAGS.
EU_INCLUDEDIR comes from pkg-config --variable, which does not prefix
the sysroot, so a cross build gets -I/usr/include and the compiler
rejects it with -Wpoison-system-directories. The check then fails and
multithreading support is turned off.

Use DW_CFLAGS instead, which pkg-config already makes sysroot aware.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Adarsh Jagadish Kamini <adarsh.jagadish.kamini@est.tech>
---
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1096,7 +1096,7 @@
 if test x$ENABLE_MULTITHREADING != xno; then
    saved_CPPFLAGS="$CPPFLAGS"
    
-   CPPFLAGS="-I$EU_INCLUDEDIR $CPPFLAGS"
+   CPPFLAGS="$DW_CFLAGS $CPPFLAGS"
    AC_CHECK_HEADER([elfutils/version.h],
 		   [HAS_ELFUTILS_VERSION=yes],
 		   [AC_MSG_NOTICE([could not find elfutils/version.h])])
